# Update 53 ceremony log

Upstream `58b08c38`, seed `B066CEB5FE8FC9E8` (3,064,878 bytes).

What was changed and what was run, in order, one line each. Detail lives in
the commit it points to; findings go to the register, measurements to
JUSTIFICATIONS.md. This file is the thread, not the record.

## Changes

- `c5547e3` bank_truth: bank every Update, keep every bank, record what the
  arms said. Retires the green-arms rule and `--keep 3`; adds `ARMS`.

## Steps

- **Read before running anything.** Fetched U53. Our four hard-coded host
  contracts hold (ram-size cell 4072, ring 5242880 / 1048576, wpos 28704,
  rpos 28712 -- same files, same counts as U52).
  - **New refusal to know about:** `opening.codex`'s entry point no longer
    falls through to `TEXT`; an unknown mode is now `CODEGEN-ERRORS:1` +
    `CODEGEN-HALTED`. The ladder sends only `CDX`, `TEXT` and `IR-CCE`, all
    named modes. Checked, not assumed.
  - **PR 98 absorbed byte-identically** -- `ZigEmitter.codex`,
    `Shake.codex` and `check-zig-prelude-surface.ps1` in U53 are our
    `zig-tree-shaking` files exactly. Plugs row 2.04. PR 95 is row 2.01.
  - **PR 96 closed as already-fixed** (their 20398); the U52 duplicate-arm
    blocker is gone at source, unverified by a run. It left plugs row 2.02
    open and unowned: the zig plug has no equivalent of the duplicate-arm
    drop C# got, so it refuses legal Codex.
  - Finding 66 is COMPILER-34; finding 67 credited by our number.
  - **Owed outbound:** U53 opens its "Open from Update 52" asking for our
    second compiler PR (`compiler-only-second-pr`, 3 unsent commits),
    reserved in the COMPILER-30 row. Needs a rebase onto U53.

- `248b938` BOX.md: the before/during/after checklist for compute jobs.
  Its After step now requires a line in this file.
- `2403dad` seed_identity: U53's release note drops the word "seed" before
  the hash, so the bank would have been named `truth/seed-b066ceb5` instead
  of `truth/u53`. Verified against every release seed 42-53; the delta is one
  row.

- Retired the `cobblestone-treeshake` worktree -- PR 98 landed, so its
  purpose is served. Branch `zig-tree-shaking` kept, local and on origin, as
  the record. `cobblestone-pin` moved off `16751b22` to `58b08c38`, so the
  transpiler's `$COBBLESTONE_ROOT` is the release we are banking.

## Steps (continued)

- **Step 2, the seed canary: GREEN.** Sandbox
  `20260829T164725Z-u53-canary` (ladder `2403dad`, codex `58b08c38`), log
  `canary.log`. One subject -- `codex/test/plug-oracle-arith.codex`,
  unchanged between U52 and U53, so the seed is the only variable --
  compiled by both seeds on bare metal.
  - Both 5.0 s, `SIZE:` declared == got on both, no error anywhere in the
    log. The new seed boots under our QEMU flags, takes the ring preload,
    and our reader parses its output.
  - **The find, before any compute:** `seed_identity.py` did not recognise
    U53's note (`2403dad` above). This is the second release form it has
    needed teaching, and the canary is where it should be caught.
  - **It previews the bank diff.** Diagnostics BYTE-IDENTICAL (14 lines,
    same codes and positions); map same 189 rows, 2 bytes; image 1,552 bytes
    LARGER and diverging from byte 9. So expect the x86/image truths to move
    and the front-end truths to hold.
  - Presence checks, both baseline-free: the extracted seeds hash to
    `61c81b04d0c3cc2e`/2,933,240 and `b066ceb5fe8fc9e8`/3,064,878; and the
    two outputs DIFFER, which is what says the `seed=` parameter was honoured
    rather than silently ignored. Byte-identical output here would have been
    a canary that tested nothing and passed.
  - `check_paths.py` reports FAIL on the two `zig-plug` build-output
    artifacts. That is the ordinary fresh-sandbox state -- they appear after
    `cycle.sh` -- and the canary is bare-metal only, so it does not need
    them.

- **Step 3, the pin: `u53-rebank` at `58b08c38`, LENGTH ZERO.** No
  cherry-picks owed -- the outbound queue emptied into this release. Pushed
  to `origin`. `ladder_status` reads `codex u53-rebank = upstream/master
  exactly`.
- **Step 3, tier bare columns: SET GREEN, 26 of 26.** Sandbox
  `20260829T165157Z-u53-tiers-bare` (ladder `85a096a`, codex `58b08c38`),
  log `tiers-bare.log`, banked as `findings/gold/u53/` (`60f36d2`). The 27th
  tier is a zig-only refusal probe with no bare column by design.
  - Presence check: **26 fresh, 0 cache hits, 0 stale.** `gold_key` is
    sha256(program text + seed sha), so the new seed invalidated every column
    and none could be read from u52's bank.
  - **All 26 columns are byte-identical to u52's.** Update 53 moved nothing
    observable in the primitive tier population on bare metal, which agrees
    with the canary's byte-identical diagnostics.
  - Carried back and verified per file by content, not by count.
  - Cost the checklist a fix: the completion watch used
    `pgrep -f 'tiers_run.py --bare'` and matched its own argv, so it waited
    on itself. `4809bfe` puts that in BOX.md beside the `pkill -f` rule it
    shares a root with.

- **Steps 3-5, the rebank: 14 OF 14 GREEN.** Sandbox
  `20260829T165939Z-u53-rebank` (ladder `fc208a2`, codex `58b08c38`), log
  `logs/rebank-20260829-170007.log`. Truth arms 12 units clean, sweep 14/14 in
  777 s, zero ORACLE DIFF, 43m32s end to end. Update 52 was 6/14 and could not
  be transpiled at all; this is the release that unblocked the zig arm.
  - Banked `truth/u53/` (`dedbcb9`), the first bank carrying an `ARMS` file:
    **agreed 14 of 14**, derived from `ast/<rung>.diff` rather than declared.
    Presence check: all 14 provenance sidecars stamped `b066ceb5fe8fc9e8`, 12
    distinct harness shas, one per unit.
  - `bank_diff u51 -> u53`: **three moved, eleven held.**
    `ir_to_x86_on_fib`, `ir_to_x86_on_cce`, `passes_to_x86_on_mid` -- but NOT
    `lir_to_x86` or `passes_to_x86_on_arith`, so a subset of the x86 family and
    not the whole of it. The canary called this shape from a five-second probe.
  - Diagnostics census: 3,110 over 5 codes, all known to `check_diags.py`
    POLICY, zero UNKNOWN. **No POLICY re-pin owed** -- it is keyed by code, not
    by count.
  - README banked-against table moved to Update 53 / `B066CEB5`; tagged
    `u53-14of14`.
- **codexzig, the ceremony gate: the FIXED POINT HOLDS.** `build.py` on
  transpiler `master` against `cobblestone-pin @ 58b08c38`, 451.5 s, exit 0;
  both passes 2,445,785 bytes and byte-identical. Committed as transpiler
  `91c600d`. Presence check: `generated/PROVENANCE` names the U53 checkout and
  the 3,064,878-byte seed, and the run took minutes -- a 3 s warm run would
  have re-checked the Update 52 artifacts and said nothing.
  - **It overwrote `generated/local/codexzig`, which safari-codex reads.** That
    slot is gitignored, so it is shared by every branch and a checkout does not
    switch it. No damage -- safari's newest artifact predated the window -- but
    the recovery was a hand `cp -p`, which is not a method: it holds safari's
    size+mtime cache key constant across a transpiler swap. Fixed properly by
    rebuilding from the branch rather than copying.

